@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="mt-4">
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
        Last updated: @DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")
    </p>

    <h4>1. Purpose of this system</h4>
    <p>
        The Contract Monthly Claim System (CMCS) is an academic project used to
        demonstrate web development concepts. It is not a real employee or payroll production system.
    </p>

    <h4>2. Data Storage </h4>
    <p>The program makes use of an in-memory database:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Pre determined users and their passwords. All are fictonal and do not represent real world people..</li>
        <li>Claim information from lecturers such as their details, hours worked and hourly rate</li>
        <li>Claim status information (Pending, Verified, Approved and Finalised).</li>
        <li>File Upload for supporting documents.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        All Data is cleared and lost when the app restarts, due to the in-memory database
    </p>

    <h4>3. Sessions</h4>
    <p>
        The CMCS uses cookies to keep you logged in. session cookies. The cookies used stores limited information such as:
        The user ID, full names and roles, as well as hourly rate.
        These cookies are not used for marketing purposes
       
    </p>


    <h4>4. Access</h4>
    <p>
        Access control is defined by user roles:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Lecturers can see only their own claims.</li>
        <li>Coordinators and Managers can view and process submitted claims.</li>
        <li>HR users can manage user accounts and view summary reports.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        These rules are enforced in the controllers using session-based checks.
    </p>

    <h4>6. Educational use</h4>
    <p>
        This system was purely designed for the PROG6212 module and its POE.
        Any and all details used were for assesment and demonstration purposes. 
        This system is intended for educational use only.
    </p>

    <h4>7. Contact</h4>
    <p>
        If you have questions about this project, the
        CMCS system, please contact the developer:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Student:</strong> Fay-yaad Ahmed Parker (ST10434066)</li>
        <li><strong>Module:</strong> PROG6212 – Programming 2A</li>
    </ul>
</div>